  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Where the state lives",
      "items": [
        "MMKV holds tiny persisted preferences; AsyncStorage is only for small non-critical data — neither is a place for a secret",
        "tokens and secrets live in the OS keystore behind the SecretStore and TokenStore ports — never in AsyncStorage, MMKV, a log or the bundle",
        "typed storage carries a schema, a version and migrations, and the migrations run on startup and on the first read"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Server state and the cache",
      "items": [
        "TanStack Query plus the shared SDK carry the server state: cache keys, retries, dedupe and background refresh — never a useEffect fetch per screen",
        "the query key is the cache identity: stable, serializable, and it contains every input the query depends on",
        "the cache is the last good data; offline is a visible state beside it, not a generic error, and the list is cursor-paginated"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "The outbox is the write path",
      "items": [
        "the optimistic row and the queued mutation are written in one transaction; every queued mutation carries an idempotency key",
        "the outbox is persisted, survives app restarts and drains on reconnect, on foreground and from a background task",
        "the server wins a conflict and the rejection is visible; the client is untrusted, so prices, payments and entitlements are server-authoritative"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
